<title>JAPAN: Tokuyo City up after problem loan details.</title>
<headline>Tokuyo City up after problem loan details.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Tokuyo City Bank Ltd rose on the Tokyo Stock Exchange early on Wednesday after the bank's announcement on Tuesday of an estimate of its problem loans.</p>
<p>Shares in the second-tier regional bank based in Sendai, northern Japan, rose eight yen or 6.30 percent to 135 yen, by 0038 GMT.</p>
<p>It was the fourth-largest percentage gainer in the first section of the exchange.</p>
</text>
